{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454686-lilith","id":1454686,"title":"Lilith?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-11T07:35:34-07:00","id":1454686,"title":"Lilith?","content":"Lilith mainly appears in Book of Nod, Revelation of Dark Mother, two Verbena books and Gehenna (non-canon now though). But what is she?<br /> <br /> I know the truth is up to you, but I always think she is one of earliest mages after reading Lilith\u2019s <b>Magick</b> in BoN.<br /> <br /> Maybe she used her magick to awaken Caine, and, as Verbena said, became oldest Wyck.<br /> <br /> Maybe she is still alive but retreated to Deep Umbra because of damn-high Paradox\u2026<br /> <br /> But AFAIK more material about her is of VtM (reason why I post here\u2026)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-11T08:45:11-07:00","id":1454689,"title":"","content":"She predates the gameline species and isn't any of them. She is a unique being from the age of myth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-11T08:50:51-07:00","id":1454690,"title":"","content":"Hrm... at the risk of thread derailing, does it matter?<br /> <br /> Much like the Antediluvians, Caine, and assorted creatures at that power level, do the specifics matter to a normal game? In a standard game, the vampires are running about doing vampire things, like arson, murder and jaywalking. The existence and specifics of Lilith (and Caine, and Enoch and Saulot and the Archangels, etc) do not matter because they are not relevant. And they are not relevant because they are not directly a part of the game. They don't have stats not because they are invincible, but because they are not present and a direct issue.<br /> <br /> So, why does it matter what Lilith specifically is or is not in a game?<br /> <br /> If I were to be specific, I would say there are multiple Liliths; a Lilith that is functionally an arch-mage and spends her time in the umbra, a Lilith that is a goddess-like entity created by worship, a malevolent Lilith that is a goddess-like entity created by violent worship and fear, and so on. Telling them apart might be difficult, until it is too late.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-11T09:16:57-07:00","id":1454692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454686-lilith#post1454686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lilith mainly appears in Book of Nod, Revelation of Dark Mother, two Verbena books and Gehenna (non-canon now though). But what is she?<br /> <br /> I know the truth is up to you, but I always think she is one of earliest mages after reading Lilith\u2019s <b>Magick</b> in BoN.<br /> <br /> Maybe she used her magick to awaken Caine, and, as Verbena said, became oldest Wyck.<br /> <br /> Maybe she is still alive but retreated to Deep Umbra because of damn-high Paradox\u2026<br /> <br /> But AFAIK more material about her is of VtM (reason why I post here\u2026)</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no clear answer in canon. That said, in my games she's a proto human, lover of Lucifer and immortal archmage that made herself into a goddess...<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, keep in mind Eve is in the WoD and she's some sort of godlike entity as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 07-11-2021, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-11T10:41:31-07:00","id":1454695,"title":"","content":"In part because of the line (I can't recall which source atm) which refers to Lilith's blood ritual on Caine as an attempt to &quot;awaken&quot; him, I have tended to view Lilith through the Mage framework, somewhat. But I also tend to view her more as a proto-Mage, with modern Mages being quite different, potentially; I'd have to learn more specifically about the connotations before definitively labeling her as one of the &quot;Wyck,&quot; but she likely qualifies if it's just a term for epic and powerful (proto-)Mages from mythical times. And of course, she has very likely become much more than human/Mage if she continues to exist in the current era.<br /> <br /> But the answer to &quot;what is Lilith&quot; is likely going to depend on larger questions in your mythos. For example, it depends on how closely you choose to hew to the Abrahamic interpretation. Did Lilith begin as a regular human woman who &quot;Awakened,&quot; some pagan Mother of Monsters, or was she handcrafted by Jehovah to be Adam's first wife?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-11T11:20:40-07:00","id":1454698,"title":"","content":"Splats are classes of beings. Lilith doesn\u2019t have a splat because there is no other entity like her. She\u2019s just Lilith.<br /> <br /> apparently the Demon the Fallen writers had some plans to eventually introduce her to their mythos too if the line hadn\u2019t been ended for Time of Judgment when it was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-11T11:43:23-07:00","id":1454699,"title":"","content":"Worth noting is that Sahar-Hannibal has a visionary, transformative encounter with Lilith in V20 Black Hand, which among other things points to her still being around in some capacity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-11T12:32:38-07:00","id":1454703,"title":"","content":"In my game Lilith was the first wife of Adam and the first woman (and first person) to Awaken. She was banished from Eden because she didn\u2019t want to be subservient to Adam (and she wanted to be on top sometimes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-11T13:14:15-07:00","id":1454707,"title":"","content":"You know how, if you rewind time, the closer you get to the Big Bang, the four fundamental forces gradually start coming together into a single force? <br /> <br /> That's basically how Lilith works. You can't define her in terms of modern supernaturals; she essentially predates all of them. She is the Mother of Monsters. Aspects of her can be seen in modern supernaturals, but she herself is simply Lilith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-11T16:59:37-07:00","id":1454710,"title":"","content":"One potentially useful way of looking at Revelation of the Dark Mother is that it's just the stories passed down by vampires who claim to believe in her, which leaves plenty of room for doubt if one wants to cherry pick what's true and what isn't for one's story. <br /> <br /> In my head, her association with so many different splats in RotDM sounds an awful lot like it's just a myth to account for why there are so many different types of supernatural being.<br /> <br /> Notably, she doesn't appear in any of the accounts of Eden given by any of the narrators in any of the Demon: the Fallen line of books. They don't remember her being there. If she exists at all in your World of Darkness, she might be something completely other than what her worshippers believe. Whatever works for your story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 07-11-2021, 09:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T00:07:16-07:00","id":1454723,"title":"","content":"I always assumed she ascended to godhood of some kind (RotDM infers there are multiple gods, of whom Yahweh is just one). She's more like a Pure One than a mage, in that case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T08:13:34-07:00","id":1454742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454686-lilith?p=1454699#post1454699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worth noting is that Sahar-Hannibal has a visionary, transformative encounter with Lilith in V20 Black Hand, which among other things points to her still being around in some capacity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or it was just an hallucination or trickery from some ancient under another guise? Up to each individual ST's shenanigans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T08:43:44-07:00","id":1454746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454686-lilith?p=1454742#post1454742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or it was just an hallucination or trickery from some ancient under another guise? Up to each individual ST's shenanigans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever it was, it inscribed the Bahari symbols on his forearms using scarification in an impossibly small script; there was some material interaction going on there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T08:47:49-07:00","id":1454748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454686-lilith?p=1454746#post1454746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whatever it was, it inscribed the Bahari symbols on his forearms using scarification in an impossibly small script; there was some material interaction going on there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or <i>self</i>-scarification while under mental (or Vicissitude) influence, among other viable tricks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T23:02:46-07:00","id":1454799,"title":"","content":"Gehenna kinda went into this and it pretty much goes 'she's best left as a mystery' rather than trying to pigeonhole her into a category. I mean if you really want to get pedantic about it (at least from the Vampire perspective but also to an extent Mage) she probably is a proto-vampiric supermage (kinda how Book of Nod treats her and there was a nod to this in Gehenna no pun intended) but Gehenna also mentions her ascended status as 'Elohim' from Revelations (encompassing gods and angels) which would make her something far more than just a mage (and Gehenna tries hinting at this, too.)<br /> <br /> I mean I think you'd have more luck trying to pin Caine down as some sort of proto-vampire/proto-mage with his super-thaumaturgy than you would with Lilith because of that. Lilith seems to occupy some sort of region between 'obscenely powerful mage or mage predecessor' and 'godlike entity' and its not clear where in that spectrum she would fall. Perhaps as an equal to Lucifer Morningstar (yet another difficult to pin down character) but that's pure conjecture on my part.<br /> <br /> Edit: Another conjectural twist on the whole Lilith angle as it concerns Revelations and other sources... Revelations suggests Lucifer and 'Jehovah' are brothers (although the context isn't clear cut here.. but that's not unusual in these sources) and given the usage of Elohim you might think that 'Jehovah' isn't actually 'God' but another high ranking Angel equal to Lucifer (even though DtF makes no mention of such) - especially since some sources (again DtF or Days of Fire) treat the aforementioned supreme being as feminine rather than masculine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25533,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","user":"Mister_Dunpeal","date":". 07-13-2021, 02:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T23:52:10-07:00","id":1454801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister_Dunpeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454686-lilith?p=1454799#post1454799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gehenna kinda went into this and it pretty much goes 'she's best left as a mystery' rather than trying to pigeonhole her into a category. I mean if you really want to get pedantic about it (at least from the Vampire perspective but also to an extent Mage) she probably is a proto-vampiric supermage (kinda how Book of Nod treats her and there was a nod to this in Gehenna no pun intended) but Gehenna also mentions her ascended status as 'Elohim' from Revelations (encompassing gods and angels) which would make her something far more than just a mage (and Gehenna tries hinting at this, too.)<br /> <br /> I mean I think you'd have more luck trying to pin Caine down as some sort of proto-vampire/proto-mage with his super-thaumaturgy than you would with Lilith because of that. Lilith seems to occupy some sort of region between 'obscenely powerful mage or mage predecessor' and 'godlike entity' and its not clear where in that spectrum she would fall. Perhaps as an equal to Lucifer Morningstar (yet another difficult to pin down character) but that's pure conjecture on my part.<br /> <br /> Edit: Another conjectural twist on the whole Lilith angle as it concerns Revelations and other sources... Revelations suggests Lucifer and 'Jehovah' are brothers (although the context isn't clear cut here.. but that's not unusual in these sources) and given the usage of Elohim you might think that 'Jehovah' isn't actually 'God' but another high ranking Angel equal to Lucifer (even though DtF makes no mention of such) - especially since some sources (again DtF or Days of Fire) treat the aforementioned supreme being as feminine rather than masculine.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Shining Ones or Elohim of RotDM (as opposed to the Elohim of DTF, who are angels) are expressly divine beings but they're more like Archons or the Gnostic Demiurge than the One--i.e., they're probably emanations or direct servants of God, but probably some way above the angels who became the Fallen (e.g., note the Archangels who serve Yahweh, so he's probably some way above even them). I would say this is the level of Celestines, with the highest angels as Incarnae. My reading was, like yours, that Lucifer was either the highest among Archangels or indeed an equal of Yahweh.<br /> <br /> It makes sense. Yahweh is perhaps Helios. Lucifer is perhaps Venus. Gaia is probably up here, too, though the Garou would be loath to admit it! Above them all is the One, of which they are all fragments. Slightly above them are the Archangels. Than the regular angels below them. And so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 07-13-2021, 02:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-13T03:37:42-07:00","id":1454807,"title":"","content":"She's a myth, a hypothetical, a counter-cultural icon. Moreso than her &quot;contemporaries&quot; like Caine. As Cainites reject god and look to Caine as some kind of Ideal for the perfection of the vampire state, Bahari reject Caine; she's a later, perhaps satirical invention that fellows started to take seriously. She fills a void; people like myths that conform to their values. <br /> <br /> /channeling my inner Tremere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-13T04:20:18-07:00","id":1454810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454686-lilith?p=1454807#post1454807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She's a myth, a hypothetical, a counter-cultural icon. Moreso than her &quot;contemporaries&quot; like Caine. As Cainites reject god and look to Caine as some kind of Ideal for the perfection of the vampire state, Bahari reject Caine; she's a later, perhaps satirical invention that fellows started to take seriously. She fills a void; people like myths that conform to their values. <br /> <br /> /channeling my inner Tremere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Burn the usurper whose mouth is filled with lies! Ahi hay Lilitu! Etc, etc.<br /> <br /> On that point, I think V20 goes some way to furthering the idea that Lilith is primordial. She's Kali, she's the Morrigan, she's Asherah, and whatever else fits. That's in RotDM, but gets more airtime in V20. Note also the new Black Hand book, which says Caine is male and female, and that Caine may be Lilith, or Lilith's son with Eve, or various other things that muddy the waters a bit but are all super interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 07-13-2021, 07:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-13T23:14:12-07:00","id":1454865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454686-lilith#post1454686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lilith mainly appears in Book of Nod, Revelation of Dark Mother, two Verbena books and Gehenna (non-canon now though). But what is she?<br /> <br /> I know the truth is up to you, but I always think she is one of earliest mages after reading Lilith\u2019s <b>Magick</b> in BoN.<br /> <br /> Maybe she used her magick to awaken Caine, and, as Verbena said, became oldest Wyck.<br /> <br /> Maybe she is still alive but retreated to Deep Umbra because of damn-high Paradox\u2026<br /> <br /> But AFAIK more material about her is of VtM (reason why I post here\u2026)</div> </div> </div> </div>I have sort of written some lore about her to link her in DTF when I was homebrewing some lore to make it more ambiguous since I gave the demons amnesia/distorted memory.<br /> <br /> Essentially the Crypters came up with a theory called the Tiamat Conspiracy, which states that God is not the only supreme being to have existed, as the Fallen notice something in the world's mythology on a &quot;primordial mother&quot; like Gaia, Nyx, Lilith, Tzimitzl, Rahab from apocryphal versions of Genesis and Tiamat which is the reason for the hypothesis's name. <br /> <br /> Some Fallen who sometimes fall to torment get lucid glimpses of them fighting a primordial monster and its children. But due to them not having any hard evidence besides the shards of their memories, most of them believe it's a false memory implanted in them so they would be lead astray from the truth or just strange coincidences within their memories.<br /> <br /> On this theory, I made it ambiguous whether Lilith is Tiamat or one of her many children.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25313-raziel","name":"Raziel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-15T11:50:48-07:00","id":1454986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raziel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454686-lilith?p=1454865#post1454865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have sort of written some lore about her to link her in DTF </div> </div> </div> </div>I usually use her in my DtF stories too<br /> Just immagine the sweet sweet irony, Lucifer went out and destroyed the Nephilim, the childe of an Elohim and a Human<br /> Then while the other were in the Prison, he chilled with Lilith and made her own children with her...<br /> Even the most calm and rational Sebettu lose it when it reads about (or hear from a Bahari or any lilith cultist) their masterwork, Adam and Eve... was actually the beate test<br /> there was another... and their memoires are... missing/been altered? about that little fact, before the simple Eve, there was Lilith, who not only became something like Them (or more) there was the Crone (who spuosedly the woman who Jehova made , but Adam witneseed the creation how she was &quot;built&quot; from inside out, organs, bones, skin last... and was repulsed, so Jehova destroyed Her (but somehow she survived and became the Crone, the Caine 2nd Gen child al\u00e1 Revelations/Gehenna/Book of Nod) and Eve... is actually the 3rd attempt, made from Adam's rib while he slept...<br /> And Lucifer not only was free, but got noce and cozy with Lilith had several Children with her and after a little murder spree, waged war against Caine... his lover ex-lover, whom Lilth made... a bloodsucker... harsh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}